                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Simple Fun, If That's Enough[/h1]\nBeyond Gravity is a pretty unremarkable game. It feels more like a simple mobile game than a full-fledged PC title. The graphics are fine for what they are, but the gameplay itself is extremely plain and there just isn't much to it.\n\nYou can probably waste a few hours with it, but there's very little here that's going to stick with you afterwards. It's the kind of game you play for a while and then quickly forget about.\n\nOn the positive side, it's very cheap, so you aren't risking much by trying it. If you're looking for a very simple, childish one-button game that requires almost no thought, this will probably do the job. Otherwise, there's not much reason to go out of your way for it.\n\n[quote=]♉[i]For more reviews like this, check out my[b] [url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/10745643/]curator page[/url][/b].[/i]\n[/quote]",
